# Micro-animations (Lottie / useAnimations)

When adding or changing **interactive iconography** (hover/click/loop micro-motion) on the public or admin web app, prefer the existing **Lottie + `lottie-web`** pattern over ad-hoc CSS-only icons **when a matching animation already exists** or the UX clearly benefits from the same style as other Fissa Lottie icons.

## Source and license

- Animations are typically from [useAnimations](https://useanimations.com/#explore) / the same assets as [react-useanimations](https://github.com/useAnimations/react-useanimations) (MIT).
- Every wrapper component MUST include a short file header: purpose, trigger (hover / click / loop), and `@see` links to useanimations.com and the matching `react-useanimations` path when applicable.

## Before implementing

1. **Search the codebase** for existing wrappers: `Fissa*Lottie` under `apps/web/app/components/fissa/**` and imports of `~/assets/lottie/*.json`.
2. **Reuse** the existing component and props if it fits; do not duplicate the same JSON under a second name.

